# Build context for the release image (deployments/prod/Dockerfile, built with
# the repository root as context). Without this file `COPY . .` shipped the
# whole tree into the image: `target/` alone is gigabytes of local build
# artifacts, and `.env` — a real one, not the example — would have travelled
# into the layer along with it.
#
# The list is an allowlist rather than a set of exclusions: everything is
# ignored and only what the build actually reads is let back in. A denylist
# leaks by default — the next file dropped into the root ends up in the context
# unless someone remembers to add it here. A file the build needs is added
# below, next to the reason it is needed.
*

# The crate itself. Cargo.lock is what makes the cargo-chef recipe (and with it
# the cached dependency layer) reproducible.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src/

# embed_migrations!("migrations") in src/lib.rs reads this directory at compile
# time, so the build fails without it.
!migrations/

# rust-toolchain.toml is deliberately absent: the image pins its compiler with
# RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN, and letting the file in would make `stable` fight that pin.
